WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.250
- All right, this thing on?

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:03.500
There's the camera? Okay.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.707
So this episode is about
how to make the ultimate--

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:10.303
(upbeat music)

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:15.550
Sure, there are great standalone
video chatting devices,

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:18.349
like the Facebook Portal,
or the Amazon Echo Show.

00:00:18.349 --> 00:00:20.318
But you don't need to
spend money on those,

00:00:20.318 --> 00:00:22.790
or leave the house to get one.

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:25.950
Step one: get an old tablet or phone.

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:27.530
If these old devices are slow,

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:29.910
reset the whole thing to factory settings

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:34.760
and install the latest operating system.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.400
If the battery's old,
just keep it plugged in.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:38.980
You can buy an extra-long charging cable

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:40.830
if you need some wiggle room.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:44.463
10 feet, everyone, 10
feet of lightning cable.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:48.160
Or get an extension cord.

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:49.480
You don't have an old tablet?

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:51.910
Buy a new one, like the lowest end iPad,

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:53.780
or a Samsung Galaxy Tab A.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.270
Step two: make a homemade stand.

00:00:58.270 --> 00:01:00.880
Stop propping up your
devices with random things

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:02.043
from around the house,

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:05.160
and instead use things
from around the house

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:06.610
that really work.

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:08.807
You could try the wire hanger method.

00:01:12.144 --> 00:01:13.227
Fold like so.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:20.400
Aha, okay, also gonna fold
this a little bit back.

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:24.150
All right, that's looking good.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:29.150
And then, this is a little
lip for the iPad in the front.

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:35.510
Doesn't look like much, but check it out.

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:38.420
Or you could try the cardboard box method.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:39.970
These days you wanna disinfect.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:43.910
Measure a rectangle that's about

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:46.937
25 centimeters by 20 centimeters.

00:01:46.937 --> 00:01:49.104
(cutting)

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:55.223
Then measure 11 centimeters across.

00:01:56.830 --> 00:01:58.730
Then draw some diagonal lines, like so

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:00.973
and then do like so.

00:02:02.026 --> 00:02:04.609
(upbeat music)

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:09.230
Just wanna make sure to get a
close shot here of my artwork.

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:10.063
Boom!

00:02:11.436 --> 00:02:13.867
Or you could try the egg carton method.

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:23.050
Or you could try the Lego method,

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:25.073
which my toddler's very confused by.

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:30.710
The beauty of all of these
is you can place these

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:32.510
in different areas around the house.

00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:39.360
Step three: install your
video chat software of choice.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.670
My go to is Facetime,
which is already built in

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:45.050
to your iPad or iPhone, but
of course there's also Zoom,

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:47.040
Houseparty, Google Hangouts,

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:50.220
all of those apps still
worked on this 2012 iPad,

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:54.140
that only supports iOS10, though
some features were limited.

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.940
Doesn't matter, they all work
with this great new stand.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:01.389
What just happened?

00:03:01.389 --> 00:03:02.930
- It fell!

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:03.853
